From 4d0101844f206feddc2ee50ee2ecd08eaad752fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:05:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/25] Show a site-wide hold as "cooling", and keep it across
 restarts

When one search was refused and the rest waited out its backoff, the
dashboard showed a row of failures and a row of searches that looked idle,
and a restart forgot the hold and started a fresh volley. The poller now
records the hold in app_state; health reports it as a "cooling" state on
every search for that site, the dashboard and /status show how long is left,
and the app restores the hold at startup.
